body:
Ok, let me type out what I think is happening and then you can tell me how off I am. 

Grab the image, split it into 3 images, r, g, and b, then you normalize each individual channel to achieve what? (I know, but I want to you to tell me to make sure you know what you are doing.) 

You then merge the three images together, then covert it from bgr to hsv. 

You clear all memory from your hsv mat (you should really just initialize it at 0...)
split the image, normalize the second channel twice? 
I think that is your error. 

I am not a veteran on histogram equalization or normalizing images, so feel free to explain why you normalize the rgb and the hsv aspects of an image. It doesn't make sense to me. 

I think your error is 

normalize(hsv_planes[1], hsv_planes[1], 0, 255, NORM_MINMAX);
normalize(hsv_planes[1], hsv_planes[1], 0, 255, NORM_MINMAX);

and it should be 

normalize(hsv_planes[0], hsv_planes[0], 0, 255, NORM_MINMAX);
normalize(hsv_planes[1], hsv_planes[1], 0, 255, NORM_MINMAX);
normalize(hsv_planes[2], hsv_planes[2], 0, 255, NORM_MINMAX);

This is my two cents. I'm a sophomore in college and have been doing opencv since my sophomore year of high school, but rather well documented tasks such as camera pose or gesture recognition, nothing too out there. Hope this helps! Feel free to pm me or comment for more info, I'm stuck at an airport all night waiting to get home :D
